This PR collects the `storage` attribute into the `TokenMap` type used in the language server. In order to do so, we are now looping through the items in `sway_parse` so we can access tokens in `sway_ast::Attribute`. The storage token in an attribute is being assigned a kind of `SymbolKind::BuiltinAttr` which matches the semantic definition of what rust-analyzer is doing. 

Also removes an old unused `test_typed_parse` function. 

@SilentCicero this (should) solve the highlighting issue with the storage token.

